or troubled me. And they took four and a  half years to sell. But they sold.
And they got made. I think I’ve only succeeded when I’ve done things I
was really passionate about.
I’m always thinking, “How do I find ă story to tell?” That’ s all that
really haunts me—that I’ll never find another good story to tell. Or I’ll find
ă story to tell, but won’ t know ż tell it. Success is something you
ë really plan for . Y our films will succeed țy’ll fail and, often, it will
have nothing to do ¾ quality of í. Y ou just ś keep
writing the best story you possibly can. And if you’re directing or
